From: Yanghan Ye <yyh94306@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 26 Aug 2026 10:37:13 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] net: pcs: airoha: use SDK RX calibration crossing search

The AN7581 PCS driver chooses the major CDR PR IDAC value whose FL_OUT
is numerically closest to the target, then applies a heuristic minor-bit
search. FL_OUT is not globally monotonic across all major ranges, so
that can select the wrong interval and leave the FreqDet module
unlocked.

Airoha's SDK RX_PRCal() instead keeps the last major value above the
target crossing and searches bits 7 through 0, retaining a bit only
while FL_OUT remains at or above the target. Adapt that search order and
remove the conflicting closest-value fallback.

On an affected Gemtek XR1710G, the old search settled on IDAC 0x580 and
failed to lock. A register scan following the SDK order selected 0x5a5,
measured the exact 0x9edf target, and asserted FBCK_LOCK.

The vendor SDK source tree does not retain VCS metadata identifying an
individual author. The reference implementation is RX_PRCal() in:
linux/arch/arm64/mach-econet/sgmii/air_eth_xsgmii.c

Signed-off-by: Yanghan Ye <yyh94306@gmail.com>
Signed-off-by: naoki66 <naoki66@qq.com>
Assisted-by: Codex:GPT-5.6-sol
--- a/drivers/net/pcs/airoha/pcs-an7581.c
+++ b/drivers/net/pcs/airoha/pcs-an7581.c
@@ -1484,28 +1484,22 @@ static unsigned int an7581_pcs_apply_cdr
 static u32 an7581_pcs_rx_prcal_idac_major(struct airoha_pcs_priv *priv,
 					  int index, u32 target_fl_out)
 {
-	unsigned int fl_out_diff = UINT_MAX;
 	unsigned int prcal_search;
 	u32 cdr_pr_idac = 0;
 
-	for (prcal_search = 0; prcal_search < 8 ; prcal_search++) {
-		unsigned int fl_out_diff_new;
+	for (prcal_search = 1; prcal_search < 8; prcal_search++) {
 		unsigned int fl_out;
 		u32 cdr_pr_idac_tmp;
 
-		/* try to find the upper value by setting the last 3 bit */
+		/* Keep the last major value above the target crossing. */
 		cdr_pr_idac_tmp = FIELD_PREP(AIROHA_PCS_PMA_FORCE_CDR_PR_IDAC_MAJOR,
 					     prcal_search);
 		fl_out = an7581_pcs_apply_cdr_pr_idac(priv, index, cdr_pr_idac_tmp);
 
-		/* Use absolute values to find the closest one to target */
-		fl_out_diff_new = abs_diff(fl_out, target_fl_out);
-		dev_dbg(priv->dev, "Tested CDR Pr Idac: %x Fl Out: %x Diff: %u\n",
-			cdr_pr_idac_tmp, fl_out, fl_out_diff_new);
-		if (fl_out_diff_new < fl_out_diff) {
+		dev_dbg(priv->dev, "Tested CDR Pr Idac: %x Fl Out: %x\n",
+			cdr_pr_idac_tmp, fl_out);
+		if (fl_out > target_fl_out)
 			cdr_pr_idac = cdr_pr_idac_tmp;
-			fl_out_diff = fl_out_diff_new;
-		}
 	}
 
 	return cdr_pr_idac;
